-- R46 - QUESTION IDS OUT OF THE 60 SECONDS for both Takeaways: plain words in THE LAST 24H IN 60 SECONDS, the yellow
-- question tags moved whole to a new OPEN QUESTIONS · ODDS BOARD section before the footer, plus a table of every open
-- question's probability move. Owner's ask 28 Nov 2026 (thread "Drop question ids from 60-second summary").
-- Early in force: update dash.rules set status='in_force', decided_at=now(), apply_after=now() where rid='R46';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Question ids out of THE LAST 24H IN 60 SECONDS (plain words instead); question tags and a table of every open question's probability move in a new OPEN QUESTIONS · ODDS BOARD section before the footer", "body": "QUESTION IDS OUT OF THE 60 SECONDS, ODDS BOARD AT THE END (owner's ask 28 Nov 2026: \"Q84, KOSPI ends below this ... it's of no meaning to me ... remove it only from the last 24 hours in 60 seconds; it can be in the part beneath; and at the bottom put a list of all open questions and how their probabilities changed\").\n\n1. THE LAST 24H IN 60 SECONDS prints no question id anywhere: no \"Qnn\", no \"[n · Qnn NET ...]\" label, no yellow question tag, no \"New question Qnn\". The bullets keep the same items, order and facts. Where a question's odds moved or it resolved, the bullet says so in plain words in one short clause that names the market, the level and the date, with the probability move when there is one, e.g. \"odds of a 9 Dec Fed hike 94% on Polymarket and Kalshi\", \"KOSPI below 4,600 by 4 Dec now unlikely: close 4,915.68, 6.9% above\", \"USDKRW above 1,360 by 4 Dec: 7% from 28% (model)\", \"USDJPY never traded above 162: resolved NO, our call HIT\". Bold, not yellow, marks such a clause. Ids print as before everywhere else: the READ FIRST box, themes, RADAR, LEDGER, trade cards, QUESTION LIST.\n\n2. OPEN QUESTIONS · ODDS BOARD. A new section with its own <h2> heading exactly \"OPEN QUESTIONS · ODDS BOARD\", printed after SHADOW BOOK and straight before the FOOTER heading. It holds, in this order:\n(a) every yellow tag the edition would have printed in the 60 seconds without this rule (odds moves, two-way tags and resolution tags), moved here word for word with its inline style unchanged: same [n] number, same \"Qnn NET <arrow>\" head, question, resolves, Implied, evidence, Echo and Priced segments, one tag per <p>, in the original order. The dashboard's question parser reads these tags wherever they sit, so their format must not change.\n(b) a <table>, one row per question open after this edition (moved, unmoved and opened today), sorted by resolve date, columns: id · the question in words · resolves · probability at the previous edition → now, with its source (market, model or desk; \"n/a (desk)\" when none, \"—\" when unknown, never a guess) · today's net arrow (↔ when unmoved) · net to date. Numbers come from the same reads as the tags and the brief state; nothing new is computed or searched.\n(c) one line \"Resolved today: <id outcome verdict> · ...\" or \"Resolved today: none\".\nUse <p>, <span>, <b>, <br> and <table> only, no <div> (R38 point 0).\n\n3. The footer QUESTION LIST block prints exactly as before (the dashboard reads its New, Resolved, Retired and Open lines).\n\n4. R33: the ODDS BOARD joins the never-trimmed list. R38: this rule overrides R38's \"every word stays\" for the question labels in the 60 seconds only.\n\n5. CHECK before sending: a script finds no match of /\\bQ\\d{2,}\\b/ in the text of the 60 SECONDS section and counts one ODDS BOARD row per open question; on a failure fix and re-check once. FOOTER line: \"60s ids: none · odds board <n> open\".", "rationale": "The owner reads the 60 seconds first and the bracketed question labels (\"[1 · Q84 NET ↓↓]\") carry no meaning for him there; he asked for the ids to go from that section only, with a list of all open questions and their probability changes at the bottom. The yellow tags are what dash-ingest parses into dash.q_moves, and the parser reads them anywhere in the body, so moving them whole to the new section keeps the dashboard's Questions page intact; tested in the thread on the 28 Nov Fable HTML (identical moves, events and scorecard). The prompts are at their byte cap, so this goes in as a rule.", "evidence": "Fable 28 Nov 2026 edition: 10 yellow tags, all inside THE LAST 24H IN 60 SECONDS; extractQuestions and parseDigest on the edited HTML gave the same 6 moves, 13 events and scorecard as the original. Thread 'Drop question ids from 60-second summary'.", "revert_if": "Revert if the dashboard Questions page loses moves on a day the board printed them, or the owner says the board adds nothing.", "review_due": "2026-12-12", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
